2026-08-17 native build fix:
- Root cause: host `.deps/` (gitignored, but copied into the Docker context) contains
  `cutlass-subbuild/CMakeCache.txt` baked with host path
  `/home/naadir/go/src/github.com/randomvariable/vllm/main/.deps`; the container sees
  `/app/.deps` and CMake fails with
  "current CMakeCache.txt directory ... is different than the directory ... where CMakeCache.txt was created",
  aborting every native wheel build after CUTLASS fetch.
- Fix: spark.Dockerfile sync step now mounts `--mount=type=cache,target=/app/.deps,sharing=locked`
  (same pattern spark-cross.Dockerfile already used), so the stale host-state directory is
  replaced by a container-local BuildKit cache and CMake reconfigures fresh under /app.
- Checks: docker buildx build --check -f homelab/spark.Dockerfile . passes; git diff --check passes.

2026-08-17 triton_kernels pin fix:
- Runtime error: "No module named 'triton_kernels.matmul_ogs'" (config.py:29, mxfp4.py:61).
- Root cause: fork code (gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py, mxfp4.py, fused_moe/config.py,
  mxfp4_utils.py) imports triton_kernels.matmul_ogs and triton_kernels.routing, which were
  renamed to matmul / removed in triton v3.6.0+ (triton-lang/triton#9186, #9539). The fork's
  CMake pin had been bumped to v3.7.1, which no longer ships matmul_ogs.
- Fix: cmake/external_projects/triton_kernels.cmake pins TRITON_KERNELS_TAG back to v3.5.1
  (the API the fork is written against; also what upstream vLLM uses for CUDA). Verified v3.5.1
  ships matmul_ogs.py and routing.py.
- Checks: git diff --check passes.

2026-08-17 NCCL RoCE provider fix:
- Runtime error: "NCCL error: invalid usage" + "Failed to initialize any NET plugin" +
  "libibverbs: Warning: couldn't open config directory '/etc/libibverbs.d'" during
  init_worker_distributed_environment (NCCL 2.29.7+cuda13.2).
- Root cause: pod runs NCCL_NET=IB with NCCL_IB_HCA=rocep1s0f1,roceP2p1s0f1 (RoCE), but the
  runtime image lacked the mlx5 libibverbs provider (ibverbs-providers package provides
  libmlx5). Without it libibverbs cannot open the RoCE HCA, so NCCL fails to init any NET
  plugin. librdmacm1 was also missing from the explicit list (its lib was present via libucx0).
- Fix: added ibverbs-providers (and librdmacm1) to the runtime package list in both
  homelab/spark.Dockerfile and homelab/spark-cross.Dockerfile.
- Checks: docker buildx build --check passes for both Dockerfiles; git diff --check passes.

