## 2026-08-18 (r29) — CORRECTION to the validation entry above

The concurrent-session claim above ("both sessions coherent across all
turns, correct per-city tool_calls ... both clean") overstates the evidence
and is withdrawn. The observed raw outputs of the concurrent runs were NOT
clean: turn answers contained repeated tool invocations for the wrong city
(e.g. turn 2 asking to "summarize both cities" answered with get_weather
tool_calls instead of a summary; cross-turn city confusion), i.e. semantic
wrongness consistent with the broader corruption still being present. What
the concurrent runs DID show: no DSML leakage into content, no token-salad,
valid finish_reason values, no engine death. The #52645(c848) port is
validated for the parser-leakage symptom only. Broader corruption —
wrong/repeated tool targets under concurrent shared-prefix load — remains
UNRESOLVED and under investigation (open: V2 dspark prefix handling,
aux-hidden/mHC staleness, fusions A/B per #50773).

## 2026-08-18 (r29 cont.) — Semantic-corruption discriminator reruns

Upgraded the concurrent agentic harness (2 sessions, disjoint city sets,
6 turns, tool-result loop, payload persisted per response): assertions for
valid tool name/JSON args, city within schema world and own session, no
cross-session bleed, requested city present in final answer, non-empty
final answer, bounded repetition, no DSML/placeholder leakage, no
multilingual soup; empty/malformed choices captured as explicit failures.

Results: 3/3 runs ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED (72 responses total, 36
tool_calls + 36 stop finishes, zero empty finals). One earlier harness
generation hit "answer missing city: empty string" once (run2 of the
non-persisting harness); with payload capture enabled the case never
reproduced across 72 responses, and the persisted dumps show no empty
messages — consistent with a transient (e.g. truncation at max_tokens in
the reasoning channel) rather than persistent corruption. Original
incidents remain distinct in severity (full token soup); parser fix is
validated for leakage, and the semantic discriminator is now green 3/3,
but confidence requires sustained real agentic traffic. Remaining
contingencies (fusions A/B, DSpark/prefix A/B) stay open pending that.

