## 2026-08-18 (analysis) — Two suspects closed by code verification

1. V2 DSpark cache-restored-prefix consistency (full trace):
   _prepare_dflash_inputs_kernel computes query/context slots against the
   UNshifted table (speculator.py:917-932); shift_draft_block_tables then
   shifts rows left by whole restored blocks (:1111-1152) while the same
   kernel shortens seq_lens by the identical block-aligned span (:959-969).
   Absolute-position slot = unshifted[block pos + shift] = shifted[block
   pos]: consistent. Unaligned residue fails closed via
   _has_unaligned_cached_prefix + target recompute. No defect found.
2. #49918 class (prefill misclassified as uniform decode -> FULL spec-verify
   graph skips state writes): _is_uniform_decode in
   vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py:3908 ends with
   np.all(num_computed_tokens_cpu >= num_prompt_tokens_cpu) — a
   still-prefilling request can never classify as uniform decode. Guarded.

Remaining discriminators (fusions A/B #50773, DSpark-off A/B, aux-hidden/mHC
staleness) all require isolated GPU capacity that does not currently exist
(server17/19 GPUs fully occupied by serving ranks; LWS template applies
spec config to all replicas). Deferred to a maintenance window.

